--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0606 asks whether producing structured-text packs ourselves is worth
it. That turns entirely on what the packless documents are: documents native
extraction cannot handle argue for a producer of our own, and documents
nothing has yet asked about argue for finishing the asking. **Nothing
established which**, and this ticket exists to close that gap rather than to
assert an answer.

**The observation, firm.** Doudou, 2026-09-06, counted over
`~/data/Zotero/storage`: **9 108 PDF attachments, 5 255 carrying a
`.zotero-sdt-cache`, 3 853 without.** That is a 42 % residue, and it is a
filesystem count, not an inference.

**What was retracted, and why the retraction is recorded rather than tidied
away.** The first version of this ticket read
`~/data/Zotero/sdt-sitter-errors.jsonl` — 12 673 entries dated 2026-09-06,
12 611 of them one `UnloadedDataException` on group-library items — and
concluded the residue was the sitter's own defect. That file was retired at
sitter revision 2.4.1, and no path in `plugins/sdt-sitter/` writes it.
Whichever build produced it is not the one in the tree, so it is evidence
about a version nobody runs and cannot carry a claim about today's coverage.
**A stale artifact reads exactly like a live one** — same shape, same
plausible content, today's dates — which is why the retraction stays visible
here.

**The one verified defect from the same read**, kept because it was checked
at source rather than inferred. `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` guards its
title read with

    if (typeof item.loadData === 'function') await item.loadData();

`Zotero.DataObject` has `loadAllData` and `loadDataType`; it has **no**
`loadData` (read in the installed build's
`chrome/content/zotero/xpcom/data/dataObject.js`). So the guard never fires,
and the `getField('title')` after it throws for any item whose data is not
loaded — caught by the surrounding `try`, which returns `null`. The visible
consequence is a **label**, not a coverage failure: the record falls back to
the source filename. Worth fixing, worth nobody treating as the cause of the
residue.

## Relevant files

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` — `getItemTitle` and `inspect`; other
  sessions have been editing this file all day, so coordinate before touching
  it.
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/scheduler.js` — where an inspection error becomes a
  status.
- `bench/results/sdt-sitter-launch-2026-09-05/2.4.1-debug-journal.json` — the
  record that retires the error file.
- Ticket 0606 (the decision that needs this number), 0699 (failure
  accounting).

## Actions

1. Run the current sitter over the library and capture its own account of
   every attachment it does not cover, from the channel it actually writes
   today — `Zotero.debug()` and the in-session ring, not the retired file.
2. Classify the 3 853 by the sitter's own vocabulary: not yet attempted,
   missing source file, unsupported attachment type, read failure, and
   genuine extraction failure. The first and the last argue opposite ways
   about 0606, which is the point of separating them.
3. Fix the `loadData` guard to `loadAllData`, with the coordination note
   above. One line; it does not need a ticket of its own.

## Test

- Red first for the guard: an item whose data is not loaded, put through
  `getItemTitle`. It must return the filename fallback against the unfixed
  tree and the real title after — and note that the unfixed behaviour is
  silent, so a test asserting "no exception is raised" passes either way and
  proves nothing. Assert the title.
- The classification is a count, so its control is arithmetic: the classes
  must sum to 3 853, and a class that quietly swallows the remainder is the
  failure mode to watch for.

## Verification

- [ ] The 3 853 are classified, and the classes sum to it.
- [ ] The count in the "genuine extraction failure" class is stated as a
      number, since that is the only class arguing for 0606's producer.
- [ ] The stale `sdt-sitter-errors.jsonl` is deleted from the author's data
      directory, so nobody reads it as live a second time.

## Invariants

- The sitter still never writes to `storage/`, never changes extraction
  preferences and never replaces a source attachment.
- No claim about coverage is made from an artifact whose writer is not in the
  tree.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The residue is classified from a live channel, with the classes summing
      to the measured total.
- [ ] Ticket 0606 has the one number its decision needs: how many documents
      native extraction genuinely cannot handle.
- [ ] The `loadData` guard is corrected.
